Fillets and chamfers: an analytic blend's contact that leaves its face
through a vertex of the face's boundary, found on one of the vertex's
edges within the vertex's tolerance, ends at the vertex (mitcad#235).

The case: the recess's rim of 0691 rounded with 1, the rib's bottom edges
rounded with 1 up to 45-degree slopes; the rim's rounding has its contact
on the recess's 45-degree cone exactly where the rib's roundings meet the
slopes, so that the contact leaves the cone through the vertex there. In
a part's own body the curve of the edge between the cone and the rib's
rounding ends 3.7e-5 past that vertex (within its tolerance of 2.4e-4):
the hatching of the contact on the cone found its end inside that edge,
5e-6 before the curve's end, and a sliver of the edge was left between
the point and the vertex. The cone's wire intersected itself there and
the result was invalid (with the curve carried 2e-5 past the vertex in
the test's body, valid but with that sliver: the area 1.7e-3 more than
the exact body's).

- FillSD (ChFi3d_Builder_SpKP.cxx): an end found inside an arc (not at a
  vertex by the hatching) within the tolerance of one of the arc's
  vertices is put at that vertex (SnapToVertex, until now used only for a
  contact along the face's boundary, with the vertices' tolerance).

Test: the rib's edges with the cone carried 2e-5 past their vertices
(geometry test_fillet_results); the result is the exact body's.

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_SpKP.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_SpKP.cxx
@@ -1173,6 +1173,29 @@
     // inside.)
     SnapToVertex(DStr, CD, isFirst, ons, pitol, snapTol);
   }
+  else if (pPH != nullptr && Pons.IsOnArc() && !Pons.IsVertex())
+  {
+    // A tangency line that leaves its face through a vertex of the face's
+    // boundary, found on one of the vertex's edges within the vertex's
+    // tolerance (a contact running exactly through the vertex where two
+    // edges of the face meet): at the vertex. Else a sliver of that edge
+    // is left between the point and the vertex, and the face's wire
+    // intersects itself there.
+    TopoDS_Vertex V1, V2;
+    TopExp::Vertices(Pons.Arc(), V1, V2);
+    double aTolV = 0.;
+    for (const TopoDS_Vertex& V : {V1, V2})
+    {
+      if (!V.IsNull())
+      {
+        aTolV = std::max(aTolV, BRep_Tool::Tolerance(V));
+      }
+    }
+    if (aTolV > 0.)
+    {
+      SnapToVertex(DStr, CD, isFirst, ons, pitol, aTolV);
+    }
+  }
 }
 
